Third-party notices for the juice-ui icons package
==================================================

Icon artwork
------------

index.json.gz embeds icon artwork from the Material Icons / Material Symbols
set published by Google:

    https://github.com/google/material-design-icons

Copyright the Material Design Authors. Licensed under the Apache License,
Version 2.0; the full licence text is in icons/LICENSE alongside this file.
Upstream ships no NOTICE file of its own (verified: the repository has none),
so nothing further is required to be reproduced.

Modifications
-------------

Apache-2.0 §4(b) requires that modified files carry prominent notice of the
change. The artwork here is modified from upstream as follows.

  * Fetched as the 24x24 `24px.svg` asset of each icon from the published
    asset URL pattern (`fonts.gstatic.com/s/i/materialicons/{icon}/v{n}/`).
  * Reduced to the inner markup of the `<svg>` element: the wrapper element
    and its attributes are dropped, as is the transparent 24x24 bounding
    shape that upstream includes for layout.
  * Re-serialised into a single gzipped JSON index keyed by icon name, rather
    than one file per icon.
  * No path geometry is altered. Colour is applied by the caller at render
    time through a theme token; the stored markup carries no fill of its own.

Icons omitted
-------------

The corpus is otherwise complete. Three icons are excluded:

  * `screen_search_desktop` — its artwork carries an inline `style=`
    attribute, which this application's Content-Security-Policy forbids.
  * `android`, `flutter_dash` — these depict trademarks. Apache-2.0 §6
    grants no trademark rights, and the licence under which the artwork is
    supplied therefore does not extend to reproducing the marks on
    third-party commercial listings. The exclusion is enforced by
    TestTrademarkedGlyphsExcluded in icons_test.go.

Icon metadata
-------------

The search terms in index.json.gz — each icon's categories and synonym tags —
were obtained from the Google Fonts icon metadata endpoint:

    https://fonts.google.com/metadata/icons

This endpoint is undocumented and states no licence terms. The Apache-2.0
grant covering the artwork repository does not evidently extend to it. This is
unresolved. Should it need resolving, the equivalent names and categories are
derivable from the Apache-2.0 repository itself, at some cost to match quality,
since the synonym lists are what make the retrieval work.
